{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "rates-project-evap-links-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.59: `rates-project-evap-links`: THC running exhaust, permeation, fuel vapor venting and fuel leaks for passenger cars at Rates scale in PROJECT domain, computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE plus the PROJECT input database `inputs/washtenaw-project-crankcase.esm` (links 1 and 2 on road types 4 and 5, off-network link 3). moves.rs captured it with the execution database named MOVESExecution.\\n\\nRunning exhaust is selected, so DistanceCalculator writes the links' distance and RatePostProcessorRatesFirst.sql's second RatePerDistance INSERT writes the evaporative rows of both on-network links as MOVESOutput over that distance: 384 of RatePerDistance's 632 rows (the other 248 are running exhaust). In PROJECT domain that is not the per-bin quotient: ProjectTAG's SourceHours on a link is SHO without the travel-time share, so the rate per SourceHour over the distance is the rate over the link's length (1 mile and 0.5 mile here), not over its speed. RatePerVehicle (128) and RatePerProfile (64) are the off-network link's, as in `rates-project-evap`.\\n\\nWHAT IT EXERCISES: `rpd_ratePerDistance`'s second arm, `out_emissionQuant / rto_distance` with `rto_distance` the cohort's SHO per real day x fuel share x link speed (DistanceCalculator.sql), and `rpdKeptBin`. The pre-port model gave `run_domainUnported` = 4 (the three evaporative pollutant-processes and the second link) and wrote every evaporative row once per bin.\\n\\n`n_outputRate` IS 824. `run_domainUnported` is 0.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "project-domain",
      "rates",
      "rates-project-evap-links"
    ]
  },
